# Local planning files (research / feedbacks / sandbox / etc.)
#
# v8.3.0 Q-5 (RESOLVED 2026-04-22): the `.local/` tree carries TWO sub-trees
# that MUST be tracked in git ((a) the full `.local/.agent/` workspace and
# (b) `.local/memory/specs/` source-of-truth specs) while the rest of `.local/`
# remains gitignored. See .local/research/v8.3.0_design.md §11.2 Q-5 +
# .local/research/v8.3.0_patch_plan.md §v8.2.4.
#
# Strategy: ignore the *contents* of `.local/` (not the directory itself), so
# Git recurses into it; then re-include the public sub-trees; then re-ignore
# secrets and runtime state inside those sub-trees as defense in depth.
# (A bare `.local/` ignore would block re-include patterns per gitignore docs.)
.local/*
# Re-include the agent workspace tree:
!.local/.agent/
!.local/.agent/**
# Re-include source-of-truth specs without re-including the rest of memory:
!.local/memory/
.local/memory/*
!.local/memory/specs/
!.local/memory/specs/**
# Defense in depth — re-ignore secrets / runtime state / per-change learnings
# even after the un-ignore patterns above:
.local/.agent/active/*/learnings.jsonl
.local/.agent/archive/*/learnings.jsonl
.local/memory/operational.jsonl
.local/memory/session_state.json
.local/memory/prefs.md
.local/memory/plugin_install.log

# Project-local Cursor skill mirror — opt-in, recreated on demand.
# Tracked counterparts live under workflow-system/agent/. Devs who want the
# skill auto-loaded inside the DevolaFlow repo itself can recreate the mirror
# with: make sync-cursor-skill   (or the project-local installer:
#   curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YoRHa-Agents/DevolaFlow/main/scripts/install.sh | bash -s cursor )
# See .cursor/rules/skill-format-rules.mdc Rule SF-3 for the parity contract.
.cursor/skills/devola-flow/
